        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0350" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg288"/>

                <head>No. 190.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 11,
                        1878</date>. (Received September 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copies of
                    further correspondence upon the subject of the pardon of Edward O’M. Condon
                    since the last dispatch in relation to this matter.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>










